resources.string:
Embed ${...} in the text to evaluate it dynamically. The prompt then refreshes per the "Refresh interval". You must first turn on "Expression injection" in Settings, otherwise ${...} is passed through verbatim and never injected.
【Variables】 ${battery} battery level (e.g. 87) ${charging} charging state (true/false) ${wifi} current WiFi name ${bt} Bluetooth device name ${time} current time (HH:mm) ${date} current date (yyyy-MM-dd)
【Network functions】 ${get(url)} HTTP GET, returns the response body ${post(url, json)} HTTP POST, returns the response body
【Operators】 == != > >= < <= comparison, returns true/false (null allowed; empty string equals null) && || ! logical AND / OR / NOT + numeric addition; otherwise string concatenation ( ) parentheses, arbitarily nestable
【Ternary (nestable)】 ${cond ? "a" : "b"} a if cond holds, otherwise b ${owner == null ? "none" : owner == "CompanyA" ? "HQ" : owner}
【Examples】 This device (${battery}% battery) belongs to me Verified via ${post("http://x/check", "{"id":1}")} This device is managed by Wang and is connected to ${charging ? "power" : "void"} ${(battery >= 80) && charging ? "Plenty of battery" : "Low battery"}
